  1165	  || { echo 'W-P1: ssh win unreachable'; exit 1; }
  1166	[ "$(tr -d '\r' < /tmp/w-p1.txt)" = "ok" ] || { echo 'W-P1: unexpected reply'; exit 1; }
  1167	
  1168	# In-box since Win10 1803 / PS 5.1 has Get-FileHash. Presence is asserted, not eyeballed.
  1169	got="$(ssh win "where tar" | tr -d '\r')" || { echo 'W1: `where tar` failed'; exit 1; }
  1170	case "$got" in *'\tar.exe') ;; *) echo "W1: unexpected tar location: $got"; exit 1;; esac
  1171	got="$(ssh win "where powershell" | tr -d '\r')" || { echo 'W1: `where powershell` failed'; exit 1; }
  1172	case "$got" in *'\powershell.exe') ;; *) echo "W1: unexpected powershell location: $got"; exit 1;; esac
  1173	```
  1174	
  1175	**W-P2 — the approved Windows toolchain, by fixed absolute path.** The operator supplies
  1176	`WIN_GOROOT` as a constant; the agent installs nothing and **does not discover it**. Revision 3 ran
  1177	`where go` here, which is the same ambient-`PATH` defect §5.0 corrects — worse on Windows, where
  1178	`where` also searches the current directory and a stray `go.exe` beside the working directory would
  1179	win.
  1180	
  1181	Exactly as on POSIX hosts (§5.0), the operator supplies **one** constant — the root — and the
  1182	executable is derived from it. Every probe is compared, not printed.
  1183	
  1184	```bash
  1185	# Operator-supplied constant, recorded on the board before the lane runs. Example shape only —
  1186	# the real value comes from the operator, and a mismatch fails the lane closed.
  1187	WIN_GOROOT='C:\Program Files\Go'
  1188	WIN_GO_EXE="$WIN_GOROOT\\bin\\go.exe"          # derived, never supplied separately
  1189	WIN_ENV='set "GOTOOLCHAIN=local" & set "GOENV=off" & '
  1190	
  1191	ssh win "if exist \"$WIN_GO_EXE\" (echo GO_EXE_OK) else (echo GO_EXE_MISSING & exit /b 1)" \
  1192	  > /tmp/w-p2-exe.txt 2>&1 || { echo "W-P2: $WIN_GO_EXE missing"; exit 1; }
  1193	[ "$(tr -d '\r' < /tmp/w-p2-exe.txt)" = "GO_EXE_OK" ] || { echo 'W-P2: unexpected reply'; exit 1; }
  1194	
  1195	got="$(ssh win "$WIN_ENV \"$WIN_GO_EXE\" version" | tr -d '\r')" \
  1196	  || { echo 'W-P2: `go version` failed'; exit 1; }
  1197	echo "W-P2 toolchain: $got"
  1198	[ "$got" = "go version go1.25.5 windows/amd64" ] \
  1199	  || { echo "W-P2: expected 'go version go1.25.5 windows/amd64', got '$got'"; exit 1; }
  1200	
  1201	got="$(ssh win "$WIN_ENV \"$WIN_GO_EXE\" env GOROOT" | tr -d '\r')" \
  1202	  || { echo 'W-P2: `go env GOROOT` failed'; exit 1; }
  1203	echo "W-P2 GOROOT: $got"
  1204	[ "$got" = "$WIN_GOROOT" ] \
  1205	  || { echo "W-P2: GOROOT drift: reported '$got' != approved '$WIN_GOROOT'"; exit 1; }
  1206	
  1207	got="$(ssh win "$WIN_ENV \"$WIN_GO_EXE\" env GOTOOLCHAIN" | tr -d '\r')" \
  1208	  || { echo 'W-P2: `go env GOTOOLCHAIN` failed'; exit 1; }
  1209	echo "W-P2 GOTOOLCHAIN: $got"
  1210	[ "$got" = "local" ] || { echo "W-P2: GOTOOLCHAIN=$got, not local"; exit 1; }
  1211	
  1212	got="$(ssh win "$WIN_ENV \"$WIN_GO_EXE\" env GOENV" | tr -d '\r')" \
  1213	  || { echo 'W-P2: `go env GOENV` failed'; exit 1; }
  1214	echo "W-P2 GOENV: $got"
  1215	[ "$got" = "off" ] || { echo "W-P2: GOENV=$got, not off"; exit 1; }
  1216	```
  1217	
  1218	If the derived path is absent, the version is not `go1.25.5 windows/amd64`, or `env GOROOT` /
  1219	`GOTOOLCHAIN` / `GOENV` differ from the approved values, the lane **stops** and records W-P2 as
  1220	unsatisfied. There is no discovery fallback and no `where go`. These are the same six T-P1
  1221	assertions, expressed for `cmd.exe`; the `go.mod` version self-check is not repeated here because
  1222	`$WIN_GOROOT` is checked against the same `go1.25.5` constant that §7's `require-toolchain` reconciles
  1223	against `go.mod` on the control host.
  1224	
