  2461	## 11. Invariants the producer must preserve
  2462	
  2463	- **I1.** The candidate enters only through a non-default input, defaulting to empty. With it empty,
  2464	  CI uses the committed pin and nothing else.
  2465	- **I2 (strengthened).** The candidate's accepted identity is three fixed constants —
  2466	  `CANDIDATE_MANIFEST_SHA256=b6f56aac…04c`, `CANDIDATE_TREE_SHA256=e6a13215…2fae`,
  2467	  `CANDIDATE_FILE_COUNT=448`. Every candidate run verifies **all three** before executing a case and
  2468	  **emits all three** into the log. Any mismatch aborts the run. A mismatch at freeze time means the
  2469	  producer is holding a **different candidate**: record the measured values, stop, and escalate for
  2470	  a refreshed accepted input and a board-owner decision — **never re-baseline silently**. The
  2471	  archive SHA-256 is a transport-integrity check handed off through the board resource in §5.2 C4;
  2472	  it is verified before extraction and never substitutes for post-extraction tree verification. The
  2473	  digest is never written as a `ref:`.
  2474	- **I3.** No job, target, or log line labels candidate output a release, a published conformance
  2475	  claim, or "rc.5 qualified". They say *candidate*.
  2476	- **I4.** 1pvfj5 does not move the committed pin. `TASK-260720-38l1sy` owns promotion after
  2477	  `TASK-260720-25d05o`.
  2478	- **I5.** The pin appears in exactly one place (`env.SPEC_PIN`). Every suite checkout references it.
  2479	- **I6.** The composite is built on `origin/main` = `17804ce`, **not** on `c06aa1a`. Building on
  2480	  `c06aa1a` would revert the pin from `00b1688a` to `e72defe` and break `internal/closure`, which
  2481	  needs `manager-lifecycle.json`.
  2482	- **I7 (premise corrected twice).** Every `go test` invocation carries `-count=1 -timeout 30m`. What
  2483	  that flag rescues is the **race** lane, which failed at the default alarm (`internal/install`
  2484	  603.306 s, `internal/install/atomicity` 603.701 s) and **passed** focused at 45 m (609.117 s and
  2485	  **1422.407 s**, gate exit 0). On the *non*-race lane the flag is margin, not a fix — the current
  2486	  candidate passes the default-timeout run at 444 s. Do not claim "CI is red without the timeout" as
  2487	  a present-tense fact, and do not claim the race lane is only projected either (D6): it is measured
  2488	  focused, and **unmeasured for `./...`**, where atomicity's 1.27× headroom is the exposure. Never
  2489	  raise the alarm past 30 m to make a gate pass.
  2490	- **I8.** No `-run` selector is added without confirming it matches a test that exists in the
  2491	  composite. A Go `-run` matching nothing exits 0 — a vacuous gate reads exactly like a passing one.
  2492	- **I9 (new).** `vendor/` is a transport artifact only. `go mod vendor` runs in the staging copy
  2493	  (§5.2 C3), never in the repository worktree, and `vendor/` is never committed. The submodule pin
  2494	  `21585d0e937cae47e54a788d8ae36b1780eae47f` is not 1pvfj5's to move.
  2495	- **I10 (new).** Native-host prerequisites are named, not worked around. `ssh win` needs
  2496	  reachability (W-P1) and an operator-installed, manager-approved Go 1.25.x root (W-P2). `ssh relux`
  2497	  needs R-P1. `ssh lev` needs reachability, an approved toolchain, and `TASK-260728-1skseh`. The
  2498	  agent installs nothing, downloads nothing, and does not accept an ambient PATH. A blocked lane is
  2499	  reported as blocked, never inferred green and never silently dropped from the evidence.
  2500	- **I11 (strengthened).** On every **native** host the toolchain is **one** operator-approved
  2501	  absolute `GOROOT_EXPECTED`; `GO` and `GOFMT` are **derived** from it, never supplied separately, so
  2502	  a cross-root pairing cannot be expressed. Before any gate, `require-toolchain` asserts, by
  2503	  comparison and not by printing: `go.mod` still requires `go1.25.5`; `go version` is exactly that;
  2504	  `go env GOROOT` equals `GOROOT_EXPECTED` byte for byte; the launcher **is** `$GOROOT/bin/go` and
  2505	  the formatter **is** `$GOROOT/bin/gofmt`; `go env GOTOOLCHAIN` reads back `local`; `go env GOENV`
  2506	  reads back `off`. The environment is **supplied** by `$(GOENVPREFIX)` around every Go invocation
  2507	  **and read back**, because a shim or wrapper launcher can override its caller. No `where go`, no
  2508	  bare `go`/`gofmt`, no inherited `GOROOT`; `make` carries `GOROOT_EXPECTED=`. Exits 2 otherwise
  2509	  (§7.4d rows I–P). The one exception is a **hosted** GitHub runner, where `actions/setup-go` owns
  2510	  `PATH` in a fresh image: those steps set `TOOLCHAIN_ALLOW_PATH=1`, which relaxes **path shape
  2511	  only** — every identity assertion still runs, and a cross-root formatter still fails (§7.4d row Q).
  2512	  Hosted `GOTOOLCHAIN=local` comes from the workflow `env:` block, not from `setup-go@v5`, which does
  2513	  not force it (§2.3 D8). Evidence records the toolchain that produced it — on this host bare `go`
  2514	  resolved to two different toolchains in two agent shells in one week, and a third launcher on
  2515	  `PATH` is older than `go.mod` requires.
  2516	- **I12 (new).** Package discovery never flows through `$(shell …)` or an unguarded pipe.
  2517	  `go list` output is materialized in a status-checked assignment and only then filtered; the safe
  2518	  set is asserted non-empty and the exclusion asserted to be exactly one package (§7, §7.4). A
